# HTSA page map — read this first

CJ runs four different pages. They look similar and they are NOT interchangeable.
Before building anything, identify which one he means from the trigger phrase.
If the trigger is ambiguous, ask one short question and nothing else.

## The four pages

| CJ says | Page | File | Calendar |
|---|---|---|---|
| **"offer link"** | Special offer booking page | `<firstname>-and-cj.html` (root) | `/charles660/cj` |
| **"game plan"** | 30 day game plan | `30-day-roadmap.html` (shared, params) | none |
| **"enroll link"** | Enrollment / close page | `htsa-enrollment-<first>-<last>.html` | none |
| **"pre call link"** | Pre-call resources page | `r/<first>_<last>/index.html` | only if not booked |

There is a fifth, built once and shared: `meet-cj.html`, the referral landing.
Never personalize it.

---

## 1. "offer link" — special offer booking page

Who: someone from the outreach batch who has NOT booked yet. They got a text, a
voice memo, and this link. Their job on this page is to pick a time.

- File: `<firstname>-and-cj.html` at repo root. Example: `jared-and-cj.html`
- Their first name goes in the page title
- Calendar: `https://meetings.hubspot.com/charles660/cj`
- Sixteen of these are already live. Match their structure exactly.

**NEVER use the word "reactivation" in a filename, URL, page title, meta tag, or
any visible copy.** That is internal language. To the person it is a special
offer. The `reactivation/` folder is internal working files only and its URLs are
never sent to anyone.

## 2. "game plan" — the 30 day game plan

Who: someone CJ is closing, shown live on a call or sent right after.

- One shared file: `30-day-roadmap.html`. Do not make per-person copies.
- `?n=Test` puts their name in the headline. That is the default. Send it
  immediately. The file is already live. Do not wait on anything else.
- Never add `&e=` unless CJ asks. That only wires the button at the bottom
  of the roadmap to an enroll page. He usually texts enroll separately.
- Only if CJ explicitly asks for a dedicated URL, copy to
  `<first>-<last>-30day-roadmap.html` and hardcode the name in that copy only

## 3. "enroll link" — enrollment / close page

Who: someone who has verbally agreed to a plan. CJ is on the phone with them.

- Source: `templates/_TEMPLATE-close.html`
- Output: `htsa-enrollment-<first>-<last>.html` at root
- **On a live call, run this and nothing else:**
  `python3 scripts/htsa-paste-close.py --ship` with his paste on stdin.
  Wait for `READY`. Game plan is a separate already-live file:
  `https://closewithcjclay.com/30-day-roadmap.html?n=<First>`
- Full instructions: `.cursor/rules/htsa-close-page.mdc`

## 4. "pre call link" — pre-call resources page

Who: someone who ALREADY HAS A CALL BOOKED. A setter or a marketing lead
scheduled them. CJ sends this the day before so they show up warm.

- Source: `r/_TEMPLATE-precall.html`
- Output: `r/<first>_<last>/index.html`
- Full instructions: `.cursor/rules/htsa-precall-page.mdc`

### THE DEFAULT IS BOOKED. THIS IS THE RULE THAT BROKE.

CJ usually pastes only **name, email, number**. That does NOT mean they need to
book. It means he did not paste the time.

```
booked: true      <-- ALWAYS, unless CJ explicitly says they still need to book
```

- Time given: set `callLabel` and `confirmDay`, the date block shows.
- **No time given: still `booked: true`.** Leave `callLabel` and `confirmDay`
  empty. The date block hides itself and the page reads correctly. The confirm
  button still works.
- Only set `booked: false` if CJ says something like "they still need to book" or
  "send them a booking link".

A pre-call page must never say **"Let's find 45 minutes"** to someone who already
had their call. That is the failure this rule exists to prevent.

