## NEVER use a real person as test data

This nearly caused a text to go to a real prospect.

**Never** put a real prospect's name, phone number, or email into an example, a
placeholder, a test page, a preview, a code comment, or a sample message. Not
Amy, not Anna, not Julz, not JC, not anyone from CJ's list, not a name you saw in
another file in this repo.

When you need example data, use obviously fake values every time:

```
Name:   Test Person  /  Jane Doe  /  Sample Member
Email:  test@example.com
Phone:  +15555550100        (555 numbers are reserved and unroutable)
Slug:   test_person
```

Rules that follow from this:

- Any page you build for testing is named `test-*.html` or lives under `r/test_*/`
  and is deleted before you report done.
- Never pre-fill a form, an SMS body, or a referral card with a real name while
  demonstrating that it works.
- If CJ asks you to verify something works, verify it with `Test Person`, then
  tell him it passed. Do not use the last real person he mentioned.
- Real names appear in exactly one place: the config block of the page actually
  being built for that person, when CJ gave you their details for that purpose.

If you are unsure whether a name is real, assume it is real.

## Never mix these

1. **No "reactivation" in anything a prospect can see.** Filenames, URLs, titles,
   meta tags, visible copy. Internal word only.
2. **Two calendars, two lengths.** The offer pages and `meet-cj.html` book a call
   on `/charles660/cj`. A pre-call page for someone already booked shows no
   calendar at all. Do not copy call-length copy between page types.
3. **Never overwrite a live page.** The sixteen `<name>-and-cj.html` files and
   every `htsa-enrollment-*.html` are live and in front of real people.
4. **Never edit a template while building someone's page.** Copy, then edit the
   copy's config block only.
5. **Templates are `templates/_TEMPLATE-close.html` and `r/_TEMPLATE-precall.html`.**
   Their config blocks hold `[PLACEHOLDER]` values. Never put a real person's data
   in a template.

## When CJ's request is ambiguous

Ask exactly one question, naming the two candidates. Example:

> "Offer link (they still need to book) or pre call link (already booked)?"

Do not ask more than one question. Do not restate the whole workflow back to him.
